  "note": "The words a presenter would circle, by slide id, grouped by the colour of the pen. good (green): the right move or the payoff. bad (red): a trap, risk or cost. warn (amber): a caveat, be careful. key (blue): a term or fact to remember. On the slide each one gets a hand-drawn ring, drawn just after the point it sits in appears. Copy the words exactly as they appear on the slide; every match on the slide is ringed, so pick words that appear once. Keep them short: one or two per point. Stat figures, the right quiz answer and the web-app reveal are ringed without being listed.",
